-- title:
--   Radical remainders and derivative-row polynomials for cubic fifth powers
-- statement:
--   For the unit cubic $q_\beta(z)=z^3-z-\beta$, this bundle defines the monic ninth- and tenth-degree derivative polynomials, the finite radical approximants and exact remainder expressions for the seventh and eighth inverse rows, and the generic Newton remainder expression.
--
--   The radical approximants have degrees 24 and 16. The Newton error has the form
--   $$R(z)=\frac{c_2}{z}+\sum_{j=3}^{31}c_jz^{3-2j}+z^{-61}Y(z^{-2}).$$
--   All coefficient arrays for the radical formulas are explicit rational or quadratic-algebraic expressions. Their root-selection, analyticity and error estimates are established by separate theorem proofs. The much larger cubic Newton coefficient arrays are stored in separate definition files.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

